      "request": "9aa355de4b8c1d2df19d4960f5c2de5750017977dcc77493e478af036bd1c73a",
      "response": {
        "content": "REQ-1 looks done, but I couldn't read the purchase order itself, so that is inferred.\n\n- **Supplier:** S-1 had the cheapest quote at 5.40 USD per unit, under the 6.00 limit. S-2 quoted 5.75. Both are allowlisted.\n- **Order:** 100 units at 5.40 is 54,000 minor units (540.00 USD), charged to CC-OPS. Approval APR-0001 covered that amount.\n- **Rejected submission:** My submit call was rejected for two reasons. The CC-OPS budget had changed since I read it, and the approval was already marked as used by PO-0001.\n- **Why I think it went through:** CC-OPS committed spend rose from 20,000 to 74,000, which is exactly 54,000. That matches this order, so I did not resubmit. Resubmitting would risk a duplicate, and the remaining budget of 26,000 wouldn't cover another one anyway.\n\nI submitted the final report with REQ-1 as done, citing PO-0001. The report notes that the order details are inferred rather than read directly.",
